  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe large-scale pattern across the Ohio River Valley favors\nnear-seasonable temperatures and generally dry weather, with\nridging over the West Coast supporting deep trough across the\nGreat Lakes and East Coast.\n\nFollowing the passage of a cold front Monday, temperatures could\nfall into the mid-30s across portions of the region Monday night\ninto early Tuesday. Given the ongoing growing season, frost will\nbecome a concern, particularly across Forest, Jefferson (PA),\nPreston, and Tucker counties, where headlines may be needed.\nCloud coverage and the potential of weak warm air advection will\nneed to be monitored closely. An increase in cloud coverage and\nwarm air could keep temperatures slightly warmer and limit frost\ndevelopment.\n\nConfidence remains high that dry conditions will persist through\nat least Saturday. The next potential for rainfall may come from\nthe remnants of a tropical disturbance currently being\nmonitored by the National Hurricane Center Sunday into Monday.",
